WEBVTT

00:01.408 --> 00:03.000
&lt;i>Previously on&lt;/i>
Two and a Half Men...

00:03.024 --> 00:03.921
I'm dead.

00:03.922 --> 00:06.350
You're in the hospital.
You had a mild heart attack.

00:06.351 --> 00:07.450
I almost died, Alan.

00:07.452 --> 00:09.152
But the important thing is
you didn't.

00:09.154 --> 00:11.721
Other than you guys and my mom,
I got nobody.

00:11.723 --> 00:13.122
At least you
got Jake.

00:13.124 --> 00:14.490
I want to have a kid of my own.

00:14.492 --> 00:17.694
You are obviously more than qualified.
Thank you.

00:17.696 --> 00:19.062
I'd start looking
at golden retriever puppies,

00:19.064 --> 00:20.563
'cause there's no way
you're getting a baby.

00:20.565 --> 00:22.365
You're a single guy,
and the system

00:22.367 --> 00:23.833
is really geared
towards married couples.

00:23.835 --> 00:26.369
Alan Harper,
will you marry me?

00:28.473 --> 00:30.573
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:30.575 --> 00:32.942
Wait. You seriously
want to marry me?

00:32.944 --> 00:34.310
Yes.

00:34.312 --> 00:36.346
Alan Jerome Harper,

00:36.348 --> 00:38.948
would you be my wi...?

00:38.950 --> 00:42.252
Hus...?

00:42.254 --> 00:43.586
Life buddy?

00:43.588 --> 00:45.688
Okay, I'm a little confused.

00:45.690 --> 00:49.859
And not like the time I-I got
that massage from that lady-boy.

00:51.429 --> 00:53.429
Look, I want
to adopt a kid,

00:53.431 --> 00:56.566
and the quickest way for me
to do that is to get married.

00:56.568 --> 00:58.768
And if I'm gonna
settle for someone,

00:58.770 --> 01:00.503
it might as well be you.

01:00.505 --> 01:03.339
That's exactly what
my first wife said.

01:03.341 --> 01:06.109
Listen, I-I know
this sounds crazy,

01:06.111 --> 01:09.579
but you would be doing me
the biggest favor of my life.

01:09.581 --> 01:11.080
Walden, there are
literally millions of women

01:11.082 --> 01:13.283
who would marry you
at the drop of a hat.

01:13.285 --> 01:14.884
Yeah, but I wouldn't be
half as happy

01:14.886 --> 01:16.920
with any of them
as I would be with you.

01:16.922 --> 01:18.821
Go on.

01:21.293 --> 01:24.460
When-when I think of
the ten things I want in a wife,

01:24.462 --> 01:26.229
you have nine of them.

01:26.231 --> 01:28.464
You're my best friend,
you're trustworthy,

01:28.466 --> 01:31.734
you're loving, you're smart,
you'll never leave me.

01:31.736 --> 01:34.437
Married or not, till
death do us part.

01:34.439 --> 01:36.606
You're funny,
you're understanding.

01:36.608 --> 01:39.142
You don't care
if I leave the toilet seat up.

01:39.144 --> 01:40.877
I actually prefer it.

01:40.879 --> 01:43.079
Although, the other night,
I forgot it was up,

01:43.081 --> 01:44.814
and I had a surprise
splash-down.

01:45.917 --> 01:49.619
I was like a
turtle on its back.

01:49.621 --> 01:50.787
Right there. That's another one.

01:50.789 --> 01:51.955
As long as you're around,

01:51.957 --> 01:54.624
I will never be the most
awkward guy in the room.

01:54.626 --> 01:56.292
So, what's the one thing

01:56.294 --> 01:59.262
you want in a wife
that I don't have?

01:59.264 --> 02:01.064
Oh. Right, right.

02:01.066 --> 02:03.967
I-I do not have
one of those.

02:03.969 --> 02:05.868
I barely have one of these.

02:08.606 --> 02:10.606
I mean, how would
this work exactly?

02:10.608 --> 02:13.242
I mean, we're gonna
pretend to be a couple?

02:13.244 --> 02:14.877
We wouldn't pretend.

02:14.879 --> 02:17.880
We're actually going
to be a same-sex married couple.

02:17.882 --> 02:21.617
And like most married couples,
we will not have sex.

02:22.487 --> 02:25.121
Not even on my birthday?

02:25.123 --> 02:28.891
Sorry, sorry... flashback
to the first wife.

02:28.893 --> 02:31.160
So, so, I can have
crazy, anonymous sex

02:31.162 --> 02:33.096
with any woman I want?

02:33.098 --> 02:36.366
No. You will still be you.

02:36.368 --> 02:38.935
Oh.

02:40.638 --> 02:43.339
Mr. Alan Harper-Schmidt.

02:44.776 --> 02:46.876
Dr. Alan Schmidt.

02:46.878 --> 02:48.177
What are you doing?

02:48.179 --> 02:51.347
Oh, just trying
to see what sounds best.

02:51.349 --> 02:53.149
Yes, Mr. and Mr. Harper-Schmidt,

02:53.151 --> 02:54.784
welcome back
to the Four Seasons.

02:54.786 --> 02:56.753
Your ocean front suite is ready.

02:56.755 --> 02:58.855
Okay, cut the Schmidt.

02:58.857 --> 03:01.424
Oh, yeah, I'd have
to put up with that Schmidt.

03:01.426 --> 03:03.459
But you know what?
I'm gonna own it.

03:03.461 --> 03:05.028
I don't give a Schmidt.

03:05.030 --> 03:07.497
What are you saying?

03:07.499 --> 03:10.199
I'm saying, yes, I'll marry you,
you big dumb Schmidt.

03:12.037 --> 03:14.203
Ah.

03:14.205 --> 03:17.473
Oh, please tell me that's
ChapStick in your pocket.

03:17.475 --> 03:20.176
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:20.178 --> 03:21.621
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

03:21.622 --> 03:24.622
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 12x02 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">A Chic Bar in Ibiza&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on November 6, 2014

03:24.623 --> 03:29.123
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:29.208 --> 03:30.607
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:32.311 --> 03:34.011
Hi, Mom.
Thanks for coming over.

03:34.013 --> 03:35.412
What is so important

03:35.414 --> 03:38.582
that I had to leave halfway
through my bikini wax?

03:38.584 --> 03:40.918
I look like a black
and white cookie.

03:42.655 --> 03:46.723
Wow. In one fell swoop, there
goes cookies and vaginas.

03:47.993 --> 03:50.627
What's going on?

03:50.629 --> 03:52.830
Is this another
intervention?

03:52.832 --> 03:56.800
For the millionth time, I do not
have a drinking problem.

03:56.802 --> 03:59.169
No, Evelyn.
It's-it's a celebration.

03:59.171 --> 04:00.337
Well, in that case,

04:00.339 --> 04:02.439
I'll have a double martini
and hold the vermouth.

04:02.441 --> 04:04.474
Hello. I'm Robin.
I'm Walden's mother.

04:04.476 --> 04:06.310
Oh, how nice
to finally meet you.

04:06.312 --> 04:09.613
You have a wonderful son
and amazing breasts.

04:09.615 --> 04:11.148
Who did them?

04:11.150 --> 04:12.449
God?

04:12.451 --> 04:14.451
Well, he's still the best.

04:14.453 --> 04:17.554
Although Dr. Schenkman
runs a close second.

04:17.556 --> 04:20.224
They are lovely.

04:20.226 --> 04:23.527
Okay, can everyone stop talking
about my mom's boobs? God.

04:23.529 --> 04:26.964
Oh, my God, that's why I had
so many friends in high school.

04:26.966 --> 04:30.400
So, what's
the big announcement?

04:30.402 --> 04:32.502
Uh... Well...

04:32.504 --> 04:34.538
Alan and I...

04:34.540 --> 04:36.440
We're getting married!

04:36.442 --> 04:38.775
Dude! What the hell! We
agreed I was gonna say it.

04:38.777 --> 04:40.477
Sorry, sorry.
I'm just so excited.

04:40.479 --> 04:44.715
Uh, no offense, but
can't you do better than Alan?

04:45.618 --> 04:48.652
Back up. You are marrying him?

04:48.654 --> 04:50.587
Yup.

04:50.589 --> 04:52.589
Ow! What was
that for?

04:52.591 --> 04:54.358
For marrying Zippy.

04:54.360 --> 04:56.026
Hey! Why are you
hitting me?!

04:56.028 --> 04:58.495
For being Zippy.

04:58.497 --> 05:00.330
This sounds great,
except for one thing.

05:00.332 --> 05:01.665
You guys aren't gay.

05:01.667 --> 05:03.300
No, we're not gay.

05:03.302 --> 05:05.168
We are getting
married because...

05:05.170 --> 05:07.571
It'll make it easier
for him to adopt a child!

05:07.573 --> 05:09.239
Aah, come on!

05:09.241 --> 05:10.641
Uh, thank you, Berta.

05:10.643 --> 05:12.209
Hold on.

05:12.211 --> 05:13.510
You want a child?

05:13.512 --> 05:15.512
Yes. I've been doing
a lot of thinking

05:15.514 --> 05:17.714
about my life,
and I believe

05:17.716 --> 05:20.317
that having a kid would
add more meaning to it.

05:20.319 --> 05:22.619
Parenthood can be
very rewarding.

05:22.621 --> 05:24.821
Some of the time.

05:26.325 --> 05:28.425
So, this marriage
is just a sham?

05:28.427 --> 05:30.861
I didn't march in all
of those gay rights parades

05:30.863 --> 05:34.331
so you guys could make a mockery
of our hard-won civil liberties.

05:34.333 --> 05:35.532
You marched in
those parades

05:35.534 --> 05:37.567
so you could get drunk
and pick up chicks.

05:37.569 --> 05:41.004
Hard-won chicks.

05:41.006 --> 05:43.407
All right, look, we're not
making a mockery of anything,

05:43.409 --> 05:46.043
and I get the challenges
that gay couples face,

05:46.045 --> 05:49.079
but I-I also know that there
are a lot of kids out there

05:49.081 --> 05:51.114
that are just looking
for a good home,

05:51.116 --> 05:53.150
and I think we
can provide that.

05:53.152 --> 05:55.118
And I get health insurance.

05:55.120 --> 05:57.354
You guys are lucky
you're in California.

05:57.356 --> 06:00.123
In some states, they still don't
let gay couples get married

06:00.125 --> 06:01.425
or adopt kids.

06:01.427 --> 06:03.093
You know, when
I was in Utah,

06:03.095 --> 06:06.596
I vomited on a police officer,
and I was arrested.

06:07.466 --> 06:10.100
Simply for being gay.

06:11.804 --> 06:13.804
Wow, this is a lot to take in.

06:13.806 --> 06:17.007
My son is going to get married
and have a child with...

06:18.243 --> 06:21.812
Oh, God, where...
where did I go wrong?

06:23.716 --> 06:25.983
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:25.985 --> 06:29.953
Oh, there he is,
my same-sex shorty.

06:31.190 --> 06:33.757
My friend with no benefits.

06:35.027 --> 06:36.927
My boo.

06:36.929 --> 06:40.530
You know, I do have 99 problems,
and you're all of them.

06:42.501 --> 06:43.934
What's all this?

06:43.936 --> 06:45.168
Uh, oh, I'm, uh...

06:45.170 --> 06:47.404
I'm making a dream
board for our wedding.

06:47.406 --> 06:48.939
Uh, there's also
a Pinterest page,

06:48.941 --> 06:51.708
or you can go to: Alan
and Walden's big day dot com.

06:51.710 --> 06:54.211
Yeah, I got the link
you sent me.

06:54.213 --> 06:56.713
Uh, I really loved
the photoshopped picture

06:56.715 --> 06:59.116
of both us peeking
around the same tree.

07:01.587 --> 07:03.653
However, you know,

07:03.655 --> 07:06.523
we're not doing, like,
a big, lavish wedding.

07:06.525 --> 07:08.025
Oh, okay, I get it.

07:08.027 --> 07:09.760
You know,
small destination wedding.

07:09.762 --> 07:12.729
Just the two of us, the beach,
wearing leis around our necks,

07:12.731 --> 07:15.632
matching linen shirts,
sand tickling our toes.

07:16.535 --> 07:18.635
Seagulls flying overhead.

07:19.671 --> 07:22.606
Ca-kaw! Ca-kaw!

07:22.608 --> 07:26.009
And where do you see this
happening?

07:26.011 --> 07:29.479
Well, obviously,
there's Hawaii and Cabo.

07:29.481 --> 07:30.914
Um,

07:30.916 --> 07:32.816
I'd be happy
with either one of those.

07:32.818 --> 07:35.786
Um, but I hear that Greece is
fabulous this time of year.

07:35.788 --> 07:38.321
And just FYI, Mykonos is very
friendly to same-sex couples.

07:38.323 --> 07:40.023
&lt;i>Opa!&lt;/i>

07:40.893 --> 07:43.693
Nopa!

07:43.695 --> 07:45.529
We're getting married
in the courthouse.

07:45.531 --> 07:48.498
Please tell me “the courthouse"
is a chic bar in Ibiza.

07:48.500 --> 07:50.400
No, it's a rundown courthouse

07:50.402 --> 07:52.469
around the corner
from the Jiffy Lube.

07:52.471 --> 07:53.737
We'll pay 50 bucks,

07:53.739 --> 07:55.305
we'll do some paperwork,

07:55.307 --> 07:57.107
and if you're good,
we'll go outside

07:57.109 --> 07:59.576
to the food truck,
and I'll buy you a gyro.

07:59.578 --> 08:02.112
Opa!

08:02.114 --> 08:03.780
Oh.

08:03.782 --> 08:05.949
Okay. I see.

08:05.951 --> 08:07.918
What's wrong?

08:07.920 --> 08:10.020
Nothing.

08:10.022 --> 08:12.022
Talk to me.

08:12.024 --> 08:13.657
No, it's fine.

08:13.659 --> 08:15.725
You know, I just
wanted to make sure

08:15.727 --> 08:17.494
this whole thing
was special for us,

08:17.496 --> 08:19.763
for you, but, you know,
it's no big deal.

08:19.765 --> 08:22.232
I'm sure we can
still make it special.

08:22.234 --> 08:24.301
Maybe, uh... maybe Jenny
can take some pictures

08:24.303 --> 08:26.336
on her iPhone.

08:26.338 --> 08:28.572
Alan, come on.

08:28.574 --> 08:30.774
Don't touch me.

08:33.112 --> 08:35.712
Look, this isn't about us.

08:35.714 --> 08:37.981
It's about bringing
a kid into our lives.

08:37.983 --> 08:40.250
It's a simple
business transaction,

08:40.252 --> 08:42.953
like paying an electric bill,
or buying dinner, or...

08:42.955 --> 08:44.888
writing a rent check.

08:44.890 --> 08:48.425
Stop me when I land on something
you've actually done.

08:48.427 --> 08:49.759
I just got excited

08:49.761 --> 08:51.461
because I've never had the
wedding I always dreamed of.

08:51.463 --> 08:55.999
Right, the wedding
that every little boy dreams of.

08:56.001 --> 09:00.737
You know, we still need
to get each other rings.

09:00.739 --> 09:02.906
We can just get something
online.

09:02.908 --> 09:06.543
Or we could go into
Beverly Hills and have brunch,

09:06.545 --> 09:08.612
and go ring shopping together.

09:08.614 --> 09:10.981
Really?

09:10.983 --> 09:12.549
Sure.

09:12.551 --> 09:15.318
Because I do have ideas.

09:17.890 --> 09:19.422
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:19.424 --> 09:21.191
Hey, Berta,

09:21.193 --> 09:22.826
do we have any carrots?

09:22.828 --> 09:25.762
Oh, wait. I've got 14 karats
of white gold

09:25.764 --> 09:27.264
right here.

09:27.266 --> 09:30.534
You'll make a beautiful
bride, Zippy.

09:30.536 --> 09:33.503
Hey.
Hey, there's my future baby daddy!

09:34.573 --> 09:37.307
If I got to listen to this,
I got to be a lot higher.

09:40.078 --> 09:43.113
Hey, uh, I got some paperwork
for you to sign.

09:43.115 --> 09:45.448
Oh, uh, and I've got some
paperwork for you to sign.

09:45.450 --> 09:48.018
Guess it's true. Married couples
do start to think alike.

09:48.020 --> 09:52.289
Maybe soon, we'll start to
look alike, he said hopefully.

09:52.291 --> 09:55.125
It's the application form
for our marriage license.

09:55.127 --> 09:57.727
Oh, look at you.
Yeah.

09:57.729 --> 09:59.663
I guess somebody's
gonna get that money

09:59.665 --> 10:01.565
for that Mani-pedi
he wants after all.

10:01.567 --> 10:03.433
Ah, you spoil me.

10:03.435 --> 10:05.735
No, I'm just trying to be
a good business partner.

10:05.737 --> 10:08.638
The Johnson to
your Johnson.

10:08.640 --> 10:09.973
Wait, that-that
didn't come out right.

10:09.975 --> 10:12.075
So, uh... so what do
you need me to sign?

10:12.077 --> 10:14.511
Uh, just this.

10:14.513 --> 10:16.546
Oh. What's that?

10:16.548 --> 10:19.149
Oh, it's a simple dissolution
of services agreement.

10:20.285 --> 10:23.753
Oh! Oh, you-you mean,
like a... like a prenup?

10:23.755 --> 10:26.056
Yup. So, it's not a big deal.

10:26.058 --> 10:29.759
Just go ahead and sign it,
he said hopefully.

10:29.761 --> 10:32.028
Why do we need a prenup?

10:32.030 --> 10:33.530
And here we go.

10:33.532 --> 10:34.864
Uh...

10:34.866 --> 10:36.733
when couples get married,

10:36.735 --> 10:38.602
finances become complicated,

10:38.604 --> 10:40.904
and this just simplifies it.

10:40.906 --> 10:42.272
Oh, does it?

10:42.274 --> 10:44.341
'Cause it seems like
it's pretty simple right now.

10:44.343 --> 10:45.542
You don't trust me.

10:45.544 --> 10:47.277
Okay, that's not true at all.

10:47.279 --> 10:48.478
Isn't it?

10:48.480 --> 10:50.914
I mean, is this what
you really think of me?

10:50.916 --> 10:53.850
That I'm some kind
of gold digger?

10:53.852 --> 10:57.387
Okay, yes, I have lived here
four years rent-free.

10:57.389 --> 10:59.756
Look, why do you have
to make this difficult?

10:59.758 --> 11:02.192
You know, why do you make
everything so difficult?

11:02.194 --> 11:04.594
It's like yesterday at brunch,
when you sent back the champagne

11:04.596 --> 11:08.465
because the bubbles didn't taste
like “a mouthful of stars”"

11:08.467 --> 11:11.334
If it doesn't explode in
your mouth, what's the point?

11:11.336 --> 11:15.238
You said that to the waiter,
too, and it was troubling then!

11:15.240 --> 11:17.907
Look, I'm just trying
to protect my assets.

11:17.909 --> 11:20.744
Oh-oh, yeah? Well, then maybe
I should protect my assets.

11:20.746 --> 11:23.013
You know, don't worry, I'm pretty sure
that your VHS copy

11:23.015 --> 11:25.148
of&lt;i> Dirty Dancing&lt;/i>
and your complete collection

11:25.150 --> 11:27.884
of&lt;i> Ghostbusters&lt;/i> trading cards
are safe.

11:27.886 --> 11:31.588
I am a collector
of '80s movie memorabilia.

11:31.590 --> 11:35.325
And hobby mocking is not
an attractive color on you.

11:36.261 --> 11:38.094
Hobby mocker.

11:38.096 --> 11:41.231
I also have one other asset
that you cannot have,

11:41.233 --> 11:42.699
my dignity.

11:42.701 --> 11:43.933
Your dignity?!
Mm-hmm.

11:43.935 --> 11:45.535
Your dignity...?
Yes.

11:45.537 --> 11:47.504
Really? 'Cause I'm pretty sure
that the security guard

11:47.506 --> 11:49.539
at the shopping mall had
to remove the bench

11:49.541 --> 11:52.776
from outside of Victoria's
Secret because of you!

11:53.679 --> 11:55.578
Mall flogger!

11:55.580 --> 11:58.248
I got to tell you, I'm having a lot of
second thoughts right now.

11:58.250 --> 12:00.750
Really? Because this is exactly
where I want to be in my life,

12:00.752 --> 12:03.853
begging a 47-year-old man
to marry me.

12:03.855 --> 12:06.289
Now sign the prenup!

12:06.291 --> 12:08.291
I agreed to marry you,
but that doesn't mean you get

12:08.293 --> 12:09.926
to shove whatever you want
down my throat

12:09.928 --> 12:11.528
and expect me to swallow it!

12:11.530 --> 12:14.564
Do-do you... do you even hear

12:14.566 --> 12:16.800
the words that you are saying?!

12:16.802 --> 12:19.869
How about these words?
The wedding's off!

12:24.242 --> 12:28.345
I can't even get Alan Harper
to marry me.

12:29.081 --> 12:32.082
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:38.802 --> 12:41.402
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪
Boy, this better be important.

12:41.404 --> 12:43.938
I just saw you
two days ago.

12:43.940 --> 12:46.708
Walden and I broke up.
The-the wedding is off.

12:46.710 --> 12:47.710
Oh, Alan.

12:47.711 --> 12:49.777
You had a rich husband
on the hook

12:49.779 --> 12:51.446
and you couldn't reel him in.

12:52.282 --> 12:53.848
What happened?

12:53.850 --> 12:56.784
Well, he asked me to sign
a prenup and I refused.

12:56.786 --> 12:59.320
Well, of course you refused.

12:59.322 --> 13:03.191
The woman I paid to raise you
did not raise a fool.

13:03.193 --> 13:04.792
Mom, I don't want his money.

13:06.830 --> 13:09.897
Never say that again.

13:09.899 --> 13:11.232
Is that a new ring?

13:11.234 --> 13:13.034
Feels like Cartier.

13:13.036 --> 13:15.637
Yes, it is.
And you know who gave it to me?

13:15.639 --> 13:16.971
My rich husband.

13:16.973 --> 13:20.341
When Marty and I married, the
only thing I was willing to sign

13:20.343 --> 13:23.611
was his “do not resuscitate”
order.

13:23.613 --> 13:26.614
Walden says this wedding is just
a-a business transaction.

13:26.616 --> 13:28.516
H-How many business
transactions end

13:28.518 --> 13:31.686
with the release of
grand monarch butterflies?

13:31.688 --> 13:33.821
Darling, it is
just business.

13:33.823 --> 13:36.824
He's using you
to get what he wants,

13:36.826 --> 13:39.727
and you should be using him
to get what you want:

13:39.729 --> 13:41.663
