13:41.665 --> 13:43.398
I'm not doing it for
financial security.

13:43.400 --> 13:45.033
Walden genuinely
wants a child,

13:45.035 --> 13:48.069
the same way that I wanted
Jake and-and you wanted...

13:48.071 --> 13:50.038
Charlie.

13:50.040 --> 13:51.873
I just thought that
after four years together

13:51.875 --> 13:53.541
that he would trust me
when it comes to money.

13:53.543 --> 13:57.378
Oh, darling, after 47 years,
I don't trust you.

13:57.380 --> 14:00.348
Maybe, uh, a-a
prenup is justified.

14:00.350 --> 14:02.050
Maybe I am just a sponge.

14:02.052 --> 14:04.185
A-a-a parasite.

14:04.187 --> 14:08.623
And-and he tolerates me
because he's my best friend.

14:09.426 --> 14:10.491
And I've let him down,

14:10.493 --> 14:13.294
and all I want to
do is make him happy.

14:13.296 --> 14:15.330
“Best friend.”

14:15.332 --> 14:17.031
“Happy.”

14:17.033 --> 14:19.734
I just have no idea where
you got these warped views

14:19.736 --> 14:21.269
on marriage.

14:21.271 --> 14:22.770
He wouldn't sign a prenup?

14:22.772 --> 14:26.074
No, he got all upset
and he threw a hissy fit.

14:26.076 --> 14:28.543
“You don't trust me.
The wedding's off.

14:28.545 --> 14:32.080
I'm going to
Ibiza by myself”"

14:32.082 --> 14:34.315
Let's face it, the man
is simply not your equal.

14:34.317 --> 14:36.617
If the two of you were
on a plane that crashed

14:36.619 --> 14:40.488
in the mountains, Alan would be
the first person eaten.

14:40.490 --> 14:42.023
On the other hand,

14:42.025 --> 14:43.825
you're handsome,
successful, smart.

14:43.827 --> 14:46.127
You would be eaten last.

14:46.129 --> 14:49.831
You're just saying I'd be eaten
last 'cause you're my mom.

14:49.833 --> 14:52.767
Well, listen, I know you're
serious about this child thing,

14:52.769 --> 14:55.932
so I mentioned your situation
to a very cute intern at work.

14:55.933 --> 14:56.997
You didn't.

14:57.021 --> 14:59.550
Oh, Jessica's very amenable
to striking a business deal.

14:59.642 --> 15:00.975
Plus,

15:00.977 --> 15:03.211
she's already visited
Dr. Schenkman,

15:03.213 --> 15:04.579
if you know what I mean.

15:04.581 --> 15:07.548
Mom, that's exactly
what I don't want.

15:07.550 --> 15:09.283
I don't even
know this Jess...

15:09.285 --> 15:11.986
Holy Schenkman.

15:11.988 --> 15:14.122
Look, I-I w...

15:17.994 --> 15:21.462
No, she'd be eaten first.

15:21.464 --> 15:24.565
Look, no, I want
someone that I can trust.

15:24.567 --> 15:27.001
That's why I picked Alan
in the first place.

15:27.003 --> 15:29.003
How can you possibly trust him?

15:29.005 --> 15:31.139
He siphons gas out of your car.

15:31.141 --> 15:32.507
Technically, I never caught him.

15:32.509 --> 15:33.841
I just assumed that he did it

15:33.843 --> 15:35.510
'cause the garden hose smelled
like gas

15:35.512 --> 15:37.245
and one time he burped
near a candle

15:37.247 --> 15:39.414
and it lit the couch on fire.

15:39.416 --> 15:42.417
I don't know why you ever
let Alan live with you in the first place.

15:42.419 --> 15:44.352
Uh, for starters,
he saved my life.

15:44.354 --> 15:47.021
And... he's been
there for me,

15:47.023 --> 15:51.659
every time that I needed him
and even times when I didn't.

15:51.661 --> 15:54.095
The bottom line is...

15:54.097 --> 15:56.097
he's my best friend.

15:56.099 --> 15:57.231
Jessica could be
your best friend.

15:57.233 --> 15:59.400
I'm not going out with Jessica.

15:59.402 --> 16:00.968
Fine. I get it.

16:00.970 --> 16:03.171
I do have another intern
that you might like better.

16:03.173 --> 16:05.139
His name is Derek.
He does Pilates...

16:05.141 --> 16:06.974
Mom, I'm not gay!

16:06.976 --> 16:09.076
